data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Let `c = cumsum(probs)`. The category for `u` is the number of entries of `c` that are at most `u`,\nwhich is what `np.searchsorted(c, u, side=\"right\")` returns. Rounding can leave `c[-1]` slightly\nbelow 1, so a draw at the very top must still map to a valid category."},"hints_note":null}

